// Values and observations
// Six koans, one file. Work downwards with ./koans running.
// Replace __; keep the "// koan:" markers. Each koan runs independently.
// Chapter notes: README.md

// koan: 01.01 — A first observation
// stdout!(value) prints a value. Make this program print the Boolean value true. The
// surrounding new block connects stdout to the built-in output channel.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(__)
}

// koan: 01.02 — An integer is a value
// Make the output be the integer 42. An integer literal is a whole number written
// directly in the program.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(__)
}

// koan: 01.03 — Words need quotation marks
// Print the string hello. Strings use double quotation marks; an unquoted word is
// treated as an identifier.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(__)
}

// koan: 01.04 — Observe a calculation
// Make the program print 5. The interpreter evaluates the arithmetic expression before
// sending its result to stdout.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(2 + __)
}

// koan: 01.05 — Ask whether values agree
// Make this comparison print true. == compares two values and produces a Boolean.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!((2 + 3) == __)
}

// koan: 01.06 — There can be many right answers
// Make the comparison print true. != asks whether two values differ. More than one
// answer can satisfy this koan.

new stdout(`rho:io:stdout`) in {
  stdout!(3 != __)
}
